instances are processed by TagUUID\\n- The `to_python()` method always returns a UUID instance, preserving the original type\\n- The tag key `\\" u\\"` uniquely identifies UUID objects, preventing confusion with other string types\\n- The test in `tests/test_json_tag.py` (line 23, 27-29) demonstrates that UUID objects can be round-tripped: `s.loads(s.dumps(uuid4())) == uuid4()` returns True, proving the conversion is lossless\\n\\nThis design ensures that UUID objects stored in Flask\'s session data (which uses TaggedJSONSerializer, as seen in `src/flask/sessions.py` line 14) can be serialized to JSON and deserialized back to their original UUID type without data loss or type confusion."}' + '\n')
